//:: cases TC_AF_3_PvlAssumeFalseGivesWarning
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-AF-3 (PVL): assume false is no longer a silent dead code marker — DetectDeadCode
// emits a DeadBranch warning at rewrite time. There is no block cutoff for assume false:
// code after it is still instrumented. Since assume false is rewritten to inhale false,
// the state is ⊥ after it; however, only an assignment follows here (no branches or
// loops), so no further Refute checks fire.
//
// Expected errors: 1 (deadBranch warning for assume false).
void f(int x) {
    x = x + 1;
    assume false;        // DeadBranch warning emitted
    x = x + 2;          // assignment — no Refute check placed
}
